  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nIsolated showers and thunderstorms may be ongoing Monday evening,\nwith a gradual decrease in the potential for further development\nfor much of the night, continuing into the day Tuesday. Overall,\nwarmer conditions areawide are expected Tuesday, with additional\nheat headlines likely. The brief largely dry period for much of\nMonday night and into Tuesday looks to end Tuesday night as a\nfairly potent mid level disturbance moves into the area, leading\nto the development of a thunderstorm complex that moves southward\ninto parts of northeast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas. Cooler\nlow level temperatures look to move southward into the area on the\nheels of this disturbance for Wednesday, with roughly the northern\nhalf of the area seeing temperatures closer to normal. The more\nnormal temperatures should hang around into Thursday as well. \n\nA change in the overall upper level pattern is expected by the \nweekend, with the high pressure center shifting eastward. This \nshould bring a longer stretch of dry weather and a return to hot \ntemperatures areawide, particularly by Sunday and next Monday.",
